<title>UK: Belgium's Maystadt becomes EBRD Chairman.</title>
<headline>Belgium's Maystadt becomes EBRD Chairman.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian Finance Minister Philippe Maystadt has been elected Chairman of the European Bank for Reconstruction and Development (EBRD), the Bank said.</p>
<p>He succeeds Ireland's Ruairi Quinn for a one-year term at the EBRD, which was set up in 1991 to assist the former communist countries of central and eastern Europe in the transition to becoming market economies.</p>
</text>
